    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe codebase already rejected same-household duplicates and had a `sharesHousehold` flag that allowed the create. I added the missing piece: assigning and returning a shared, stable `householdId`.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `householdId` string to the `Owner` schema (returned, not part of create input), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 Added a persisted `household_id` column with getter/setter (needed because `GET /api/owners/{id}` re-reads from the DB).\n\n3. **DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `household_id` column. Tests run on hsqldb.\n\n4. **`HouseholdMatcher`** (new) \u2014 Single home for household logic: the lenient last-name + address normalization (extracted from the old duplicate checker so it's not duplicated), `findMembers(candidate)`, and a deterministic `householdId(candidate)` derived from the normalized key (so every member resolves to the identical value \u2014 a genuinely stable shared identifier).\n\n5. **`HouseholdDuplicateChecker`** \u2014 Slimmed to delegate to `HouseholdMatcher` (`isDuplicate = members not empty`), removing the copied normalization code.\n\n6. **`HouseholdAssigner`** (new) \u2014 Tags the new owner with the shared id and back-fills the same value onto existing members that lack one, so \"both\" owners end up carrying the identical `householdId`.\n\n7. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 When the owner duplicates an existing household: reject unless `sharesHousehold` is set; otherwise assign the shared household id before saving.\n\n8. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 Ignored `householdId` on the `OwnerFields \u2192 Owner` mapping (it's server-assigned), matching the existing pattern.\n\nEach unit keeps a single responsibility: matching/deriving is read-only in `HouseholdMatcher`, the duplicate check and the assignment are thin components over it, and the controller just orchestrates. Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
